  "meta": {
    "appVersion": "0.1.0-alpha",
    "author": "Optibench examples",
    "created": "2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z",
    "description": "Classic NE555 astable multivibrator. C1 charges through RA + RB and discharges through RB into the DIS pin, so the output is high for 0.693 (RA + RB) C and low for 0.693 RB C: with RA = 10 k, RB = 33 k and C1 = 10 uF that is about 0.30 s high / 0.23 s low (~1.9 Hz). TRIG and THR are tied together; RESET is tied to the 9 V rail. The output drives a red LED through a 330 ohm resistor (~17 mA; the bipolar 555 output sits ~1.4 V below the rail when high). Probes show the capacitor voltage swinging between 1/3 and 2/3 of the supply and the square-wave output.",
    "dimension": "2d",
    "modified": "2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z",
    "title": "Blinking LED (555 astable)"
  },
